          "line": 265,
          "text": "npx shadcn@latest registry validate owner/repo"
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/rules/base-vs-radix.md",
          "line": 3,
          "text": "API differences between `base` and `radix`. Check the `base` field from `npx shadcn@latest info`."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/rules/chat.md",
          "line": 6,
          "text": "Install: `npx shadcn@latest add message-scroller message bubble attachment marker trace code-block`"
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 12,
          "text": "> **IMPORTANT:** Run all CLI commands using the project's package runner: `npx shadcn@latest`, `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest`, or `bunx --bun shadcn@latest` — based on the project's `packageManager`. Examples below use `npx shadcn@latest` but substitute the correct runner for the project."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 20,
          "text": "The JSON above contains the project config and installed components. Use `npx shadcn@latest docs <component>` to get documentation and example URLs for any component."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 24,
          "text": "1. **Use existing components first.** Use `npx shadcn@latest search` to check registries before writing custom UI. Check community registries too."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 55,
          "text": "- **Use `asChild` (radix) or `render` (base) for custom triggers.** Check `base` field from `npx shadcn@latest info`. → [base-vs-radix.md](./rules/base-vs-radix.md)"
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 89,
          "text": "- **Never decode preset codes or build preset URLs manually.** Use `npx shadcn@latest preset decode <code>`, `preset url <code>`, or `preset open <code>`. For project-aware preset detection, use `npx shadcn@latest preset resolve`."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 90,
          "text": "- **Apply preset codes directly with the CLI.** Use `npx shadcn@latest apply <code>` for existing projects, or `npx shadcn@latest init --preset <code>` when initializing."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 164,
          "text": "- **`preset`** → resolved preset code and values for the current project. Use `npx shadcn@latest preset resolve --json` when you only need preset information."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 170,
          "text": "Run `npx shadcn@latest docs <component>` to get the URLs for a component's documentation, examples, and API reference. Fetch these URLs to get the actual content."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 173,
          "text": "npx shadcn@latest docs button dialog select"
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 176,
          "text": "**When creating, fixing, debugging, or using a component, always run `npx shadcn@latest docs` and fetch the URLs first.** This ensures you're working with the correct API and usage patterns rather than guessing."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 180,
          "text": "1. **Get project context** — already injected above. Run `npx shadcn@latest info` again if you need to refresh."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 182,
          "text": "3. **Find components** — `npx shadcn@latest search`."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 183,
          "text": "4. **Get docs and examples** — run `npx shadcn@latest docs <component>` to get URLs, then fetch them. Use `npx shadcn@latest view` to browse registry items you haven't installed. To preview changes to installed components, use `npx shadcn@latest add --diff`."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 184,
          "text": "5. **Install or update** — `npx shadcn@latest add`. When updating existing components, use `--dry-run` and `--diff` to preview changes first (see [Updating Components](#updating-components) below)."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 185,
          "text": "6. **Fix imports in third-party components** — After adding components from community registries (e.g. `@bundui`, `@magicui`), check the added non-UI files for hardcoded import paths like `@/components/ui/...`. These won't match the project's actual aliases. Use `npx shadcn@latest info` to get the c"
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 189,
          "text": "- **Inspect current preset**: `npx shadcn@latest preset resolve`. Use `--json` when you need structured values."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 190,
          "text": "- **Inspect incoming preset**: `npx shadcn@latest preset decode <code>`. Use `preset url <code>` or `preset open <code>` to share or open the preset builder."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 191,
          "text": "- **Overwrite**: `npx shadcn@latest apply <code>`. Overwrites detected components, fonts, and CSS variables."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 192,
          "text": "- **Partial**: `npx shadcn@latest apply <code> --only theme,font`. Updates only the selected preset parts without reinstalling UI components. Supported values are `theme` and `font`; comma-separated combinations are allowed. `icon` is intentionally not supported, because icon changes may require ful"
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 193,
          "text": "- **Merge**: `npx shadcn@latest init --preset <code> --force --no-reinstall`, then run `npx shadcn@latest info` to list installed components, then for each installed component use `--dry-run` and `--diff` to [smart merge](#updating-components) it individually."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 194,
          "text": "- **Skip**: `npx shadcn@latest init --preset <code> --force --no-reinstall`. Only updates config and CSS, leaves components as-is."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 212,
          "text": "1. Run `npx shadcn@latest add <component> --dry-run` to see all files that would be affected."
        },
        {
          "from": "skills/shadcn/SKILL.md",
          "line": 213,
          "text": "2. For each file, run `npx shadcn@latest add <component> --diff <file>` to see what changed upstream vs local."
        },
